markovianprotocol.com/witness

This is a witness for transparency logs (https://c2sp.org/tlog-witness).
Before it signs a log's latest state, it checks the log's signature against
a key it already holds, and checks that the new version only adds to every
version it signed before.

Log keys can be Ed25519 or, since 26 October 2026, ML-DSA-44 (signed
as in https://c2sp.org/tlog-cosignature). This witness cosigns in Ed25519.

Verifier key:

  markovianprotocol.com/witness+41b8827f+BJKLl8rBYM0oUxSaWh9rjTldTprEpYj/SWVIGgacA9XC

What a signature from this witness means: at the time it signed, this
witness saw this state, the log's signature checked out against the pinned
key, and the log only grew from everything this witness signed for it
before. That's all. It says nothing about whether what's in the log is true.

When it refuses, and the code it answers with:
  404  a log it doesn't know
  403  a signature that doesn't check out against the pinned key
  409  an out-of-date starting size (the reply says the size we have)
  422  a version that doesn't follow from what we signed: a different
       fingerprint at a size we already signed, a size-0 state whose
       fingerprint isn't the empty-log one (SHA-256("")), a fingerprint
       not written in standard base64, or a log smaller than one we
       already signed

Updates are all-or-nothing, so this witness never signs two conflicting
versions of the same log. If a log offers a second fingerprint for a size
we already signed, we keep both signed notes and publish them at
/equivocations. Refusing is what the protocol asks for, but the pair is the
only evidence that outlasts the request.

Endpoints:
  POST https://witness.markovianprotocol.com/add-checkpoint
  GET  https://witness.markovianprotocol.com/checkpoints
  GET  https://witness.markovianprotocol.com/equivocations
  GET  https://witness.markovianprotocol.com/<sha256(origin) lowercase hex>/history
  GET  https://witness.markovianprotocol.com/<sha256(origin) lowercase hex>/checkpoint
The same endpoints are reachable under https://markovianprotocol.com/witness/...

Which logs it signs for: it follows three witness-network.org lists, refreshed
every hour: testing/log-list.1 and both staging lists (log-list-10qps-4klogs.1 and
log-list-100qps-40klogs.1) from transparency-dev/witness-network. New logs on those
lists get added automatically. A log that's already set up is never removed or
re-keyed because a list changed. Being set up means this witness will accept and
sign states the log sends it; it doesn't mean this witness goes and fetches them.

How often a fetched log gets signed: the fetcher is scheduled every 15 minutes, but
each run goes through every log in turn, and a big one takes longer than 15 minutes.
So the real gap is longer than the schedule, and longest for the busiest logs. Over
the 30 hours to 2026-09-17, on the fastest-growing log here (Android's google1p APK
log, 29 signatures), it was 15 minutes at best, 38 typically, 225 at worst. Don't
take that from this page: every signature is served with its time at /history, so
you can measure the gap for any log here yourself.

